  "memories": [
    {
      "entity_ids": [],
      "id": "mem_1784400274109_573",
      "importance": 5,
      "location": "",
      "source": "manual",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "i've been researching the blackwood disappearance for six months. seven people, 1891, door barred from inside. miki came with me — she's nervous but her ear for detail is useful. the front door lock has a skull-shaped keyhole. that's where we start.",
      "tick": 0,
      "timestamp": 1784400274.1090274,
      "type": "observation"
    },
    {
      "entity_ids": [],
      "id": "mem_1785444264730_191",
      "importance": 5,
      "location": "",
      "source": "manual",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "the front door is a dead end. skull-shaped lock, no key, no obvious mechanism to bypass. the foyer has been searched — calling cards, coat rack, vase, nothing that fits. the library is the next logical step. augustus blackwood was a collector; if there's a key or artifact that fits that lock, it'll be in his study. miki's following me in. good. i don't want her wandering off alone",
      "tick": 0,
      "timestamp": 1785444264.7303083,
      "type": "observation"
    },
    {
      "entity_ids": [],
      "id": "mem_1785444901300_169",
      "importance": 5,
      "location": "",
      "source": "manual",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "floor-to-ceiling bookshelves, leather-bound volumes, an oak desk buried under papers and instruments. this was augustus blackwood's private study, i'd bet on it. that desk needs a thorough search — maps, correspondence, anything with a date or a lock diagram. one bookcase looks wrong, spines slightly off. could be a hidden passage, could be nothing. documenting everything. the metallic smell is unusual — not iron, not copper. something else. filing that for later.",
      "tick": 0,
      "timestamp": 1785444901.3008292,
      "type": "observation"
    }
  ],
